==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|dʰeh₁}}
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ἀντί||against}} + {{m|grc|θέσις||position}}. Surface analysis {{prefix|anti|thesis|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ænˈtɪ.θə.sɪs/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-antithesis.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

{{examples-right|sense=rhetoric|examples=[[w:Abraham Lincoln|Abraham Lincoln]], ''[[s:Gettysburg Address|Gettysburg Address]]'' (1863)<br>The world will little note, nor long remember what we say here, but it can never forget what they did here.}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|antitheses}}

# A [[proposition]] that is the [[diametric]] [[opposite]] of some other proposition.
# {{lb|en|rhetoric}} A device by which two contrasting ideas are [[juxtaposed]] in [[parallel]] form.

